        "question": "What is the most frequent mistake students make regarding the post-breakup health checkup: starting fresh with clean confidence?",
        "answer": "The most common error is making assumptions without explicit, open communication. When students avoid honest conversations due to fear of awkwardness or conflict, minor friction compounds into major resentment. Establishing mutual expectations early prevents unnecessary misunderstandings. Prioritizing mutual health transparency, utilizing confidential medical resources, and practicing consistent protection protects both your future and your peace of mind."
