        "question": "What is the most frequent mistake students make regarding the healing timeline: how long does it really take to get over love??",
        "answer": "The most common error is making assumptions without explicit, open communication. When students avoid honest conversations due to fear of awkwardness or conflict, minor friction compounds into major resentment. Establishing mutual expectations early prevents unnecessary misunderstandings. Evaluating personal growth honestly, refusing to settle for familiar toxicity, and maintaining dignified boundaries protects your emotional health and academic future."
